sase_sizes.md` long note [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parented by `sase/memory/sase_beads.md` and make it the only place [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-size guidance lives.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Required tale size in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-tale-size[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-tale-size: require and validate a tale plan's `size` frontmatter in[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sase-core plan validator, expose it on the wire, and release it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt tale size in sase[/bold #D7AFFF]                                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]plan-size-adopt[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sizes-memory, core-tale-size[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan-size-adopt: raise the sase-core floor, plumb the validated tale [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`size` through the Python adapter, and point every remaining size [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instruction at the memory note.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retire the coder alias bucket[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]coder-alias[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plan-size-adopt[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]coder-alias: delete the `coder` and `<provider>_coder` implicit aliases [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and route coder follow-ups through the phase-worker alias for the tale [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan's size.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Verify plan handoff for large task beads[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]task-plan-handoff[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]task-plan-handoff: audit and 